    "final_answer": "I have gathered enough information to provide a comprehensive answer. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n## Summary of Route Options from Central Park Zoo to Broadway Theatre:\n\n**Routes with 0 walking:**\n- **Driving (驾车)**: 7 min, 1.0 mile, via W 59th St/Central Park S and 7th Ave (has tolls)\n- **Cycling (骑车)**: 9 min, 1.2 mile\n\n**Public Transit options (with walking):**\n- **M4 bus + E Line subway**: 17 min total, **~6 min walking** (LEAST among transit options)\n- **N Line / R Line subway**: 12 min total, ~9 min walking\n- **M31 / M57 bus**: 18 min total, ~13 min walking\n\n**Walking only**: 20 min, 0.9 mile via 7th Ave\n\n## Answer:\n\nThe route with the **least amount of walking** from Central Park Zoo to the Broadway Theater in New York is:\n\n🚗 **Driving (驾车)** - **0 minutes of walking**, the absolute minimum. This is also the fastest route at **7 minutes**, traveling 1.0 mile via W 59th St/Central Park S and 7th Ave (note: there are tolls on this route).\n\n🚲 **Cycling (骑车)** also has 0 minutes of walking, taking 9 minutes for 1.2 miles.\n\nIf you prefer **public transit with the least walking**, the best option is the **M4 bus + E Line subway route** with approximately **6 minutes of walking** (17 minutes total). This involves a short 2-minute walk to the M4 bus stop at 5 Av/E 63 St, riding the bus to 5 Av/W 52 St, then walking 2 minutes to the subway station at 5 Av/53 St, taking the E Line to 7th Avenue, and finally a 2-minute walk to Broadway Theatre.",
